            <div xml:id="d159">

                <pb facs="0162" n="150" sameAs="frus:frus1943v04/pg150"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.01/383: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador to the Greek Government in Exile</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Kirk</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-09-04T17:00:00+03:00">September 4,
                            1943—5 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 4—3:47 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Greek Series 57. My Greek Series 52, August 31, 9 a.m. Prime Minister has advised
                    me that when Churchill’s two messages to the King were presented to the Greek
                    Cabinet yesterday afternoon Republican members reacted heatedly bandying threats
                    of resignation but that while one or two resignations may materialize in his
                    opinion it is likely that a solution will be found and calm restored within a
                    few days.</p>
                <p>According to a member of the Foreign Office, the realization of the effect which
                    would be caused in British circles and inside Greece by their resigning on
                    account of a statement by Churchill is acting as a deterrent to the opposition
                    members carrying out their threat.</p>
                <p>Prime Minister also remarked that the delay in the receipt of the President’s
                    reply is occasioning talk in Republican quarters of a divergence between British
                    and American views.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
